# Allowlist, not a blocklist (2026-11-15, ADR-013 in the vault decision log).
#
# Without this file every `vercel --prod` uploaded the whole working directory
# to Vercel's build machine: .claude/ (session handoff), CLAUDE.md, the GEO
# audit reports, docs/, and any untracked file in the repo root (daily reports,
# Search Console exports). None was served — only public/ is — but none needed
# to leave the machine. Ignoring everything and admitting what the build reads
# means a new stray file stays local by default.
#
# If the build starts needing a new top-level file, add it here. A preview
# deploy (`vercel --yes`, no --prod) shows whether the build still passes.
/*
!/app
!/public
!/scripts
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/next.config.js
!/next-env.d.ts
!/tsconfig.json
!/tailwind.config.ts
!/postcss.config.js
!/eslint.config.mjs
!/vercel.json
